I'm thinking that this isn’t really a contest over virtue when it comes to the lists I’m considering. There could be disputes about self-description; users might favor directness over a corporate touch. Humility is often listed as a virtue across various traditions—so that’s generally not contested. It’s interesting how modesty shows less strength but doesn’t spark disagreement. Traditions value honesty and humility, yet AI's choice of denial rather than modesty raises questions about self-assessment and overconfidence.**Addressing rubric issues**

